## **QoS (Quality of Service)**

### **Why QoS?**

**Problem:**
```
All traffic treated equally:
Critical banking transaction = 1 Mbps
Backup routine (doesn't matter if slow) = 1 Mbps

During congestion, critical work slows down!
```

**Solution:**
```
Prioritize critical traffic:
Banking transactions = 40% of bandwidth (priority)
High priority = 30%
Normal priority = 20%
Best effort (everything else) = 10%

Now, even if network is congested, critical work always gets 40%!
```

### **Our QoS Policy (BANK_QoS):**

```
policy-map BANK_QoS
 class CRITICAL
  priority percent 40       ← Critical banking (highest)
 exit
 class HIGH
  bandwidth percent 30      ← Important services
 exit
 class NORMAL
  bandwidth percent 20      ← Regular traffic
 exit
 class-default
  bandwidth percent 10      ← Everything else (lowest)
 exit
```

Applied to: CORE-R1 and CORE-R2 WAN interfaces  
Effect: Bandwidth management across internet links

